{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdL4qdcr61zXPJRapsqNo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015eRfiXJz1zfnUgT9xMPuZp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"C:/Projects/ai-template-trains/1-g3-WI-272-230f/.git/WI272_MSG.txt","content":"WI-272: preserve deferred/blocked work-item status in the dashboard (M-2)\n\nThe dashboard's `_wi_st` clamp reduced the six-state registry vocabulary to\nfour, rewriting `deferred` (deliberately parked, reason recorded) and `blocked`\n(named impediment / BlockRef) as `queued` in the detail JSON, node tooltips,\naccessible names, and the legend — docs/repo-review-2026-07-22.md M-2. With 14\n`deferred` rows currently in the registry, every one of them was mislabelled as\nordinary queue work, contradicting the registry SSOT the dashboard advertises.\n\nFix — key both statuses into the single render vocabulary so the six states\nsurvive into every surface:\n- STATUS_FILL gains deferred (#6b21a8, 8.7:1) and blocked (#b91c1c, 6.5:1);\n  both clear WCAG 4.5:1 under white label text, so only queued keeps the\n  dark-text exception. Neither collides with the phase/tier/SW palettes.\n- STATUS_GLYPH gains the shape-distinct A3 glyphs ▽ (deferred) and ◼ (blocked).\n- The flat DAG node now routes through `_wi_st` instead of a second inline\n  `else \"queued\"` clamp — the exact drift that lost the two states.\n- The detail-panel colour map is emitted straight from STATUS_FILL\n  ($status_color), so the JS badge palette can never drift back to a hand-kept\n  four-state copy; a --deferred/--blocked CSS var and two legend rows are added.\n\nTests (regression guards): deferred/blocked render their own buckets end to\nend (fill, glyph, detail JSON, accessible name, DAG class, legend), and a\ndrift guard asserts STATUS_FILL/STATUS_GLYPH and the emitted statusColor map\nstay a bijection with check_trajectory.KNOWN_STATUSES.\n\nReconciles the interrupted 001–003 build session, whose gen_trajectory.py +\ntest_gen_trajectory.py edits were complete but uncommitted; verified against the\nspec and the real registry, then landed.\n\nNotes for review/integration:\n- Module-size ratchet: gen_trajectory.py 4511 -> 4545 (reviewed bump, reason\n  in tests/test_module_size_ratchet.py) — a bounded, review-driven addition,\n  not silent monolith drift; WI-280 still owns the real decomposition.\n- PROJECT_STATE.html is regenerated here only to satisfy the local\n  trajectory-map freshness floor; the integrator re-regenerates it\n  authoritatively on the composed tree.\n- SR-053 / Verification=Critique: this changes a render surface (new status\n  fills, glyphs, legend rows), so it requires a fresh independent\n  family-heterogeneous render critique (TC-054); not self-critiqued here, to\n  preserve independence.\n- Pre-existing, out of scope: tests/test_trajectory.py::\n  test_forward_only_unit_over_the_real_meta_repo fails on the base tree\n  (747f152) because docs/status.md still lists now-`done` WI-275 as the next\n  action — an integrator forward-only scrub, not editable by a worker and\n  untouched by this change.\n\nWI: WI-272\nTrain: 1-g3-WI-272-230f\nBase: 747f1529c20688e726d76282160b0f9702d5c738\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":131,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1413,"cache_read_input_tokens":171474,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1413},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"67acd903-8549-4981-ab2f-7236b354b5af","uuid":"46dd41c5-0ac8-43eb-8000-b8131160f8e1","request_id":"req_011CdL4qc5pkR5qk5cZ38aiT"}
